This quest, although seamingly hard at first, was pretty easy once I found the right tactic.

I replaced my arcane shot with rank 3 arcane shot on my action bar.&nbsp; Being it new years, I filled a festive mug, because those give you a Light Headed effect when drank.&nbsp; That makes you slow fall for 30 seconds.&nbsp; I transported up to the top of the mountain and summoned him.&nbsp; After summoning I immidiatley drank the festive mug drink. Then I ran north and RAN (not jumped) off the mountain, and shot him a few times on the way down with Arcane and Silence Shot (hes immune to sdilence, but the damage keeps him aggroed)&nbsp; I hit the spot with the return beacon, and kept running north.&nbsp; Once on the ground I proceeded to kite him normally to Stonard.&nbsp; Occasionally he casts Mana Burn, but if you stay far enough ahead of him it will cancel the cast, and keep him running after you.&nbsp; 

Once at Stonard, I kept aggro and let the guards beat him down.&nbsp; He will summon 2 friends, but they last a max of 30 seconds.&nbsp; I kited him through the inn, which gave me time to bandage and such, because of LoS issues. 

Overall, if you can kite him to Stonard and keep DPS'ing him and keep aggro, you should be fine.&nbsp; 

I used 1 major mana pot during the whole thing.&nbsp; Not too tough, but a good challenge for a kiter.&nbsp; 

Have fun!

I started out killing Young Reef Crawlers, it took me about twenty minutes to get only two crawler legs.&nbsp; I moved up the coast North, closer to the actual Buzzbox (sort of like the quest says) and I got four in a row.&nbsp; 
Plus, the Young Reef Crawlers run away when they're almost dead, so they're a bit of a pain - The Pygmy Tide Crawlers just stand there and take it basically.
[b]The coordinates I was at when I got four in a row are: 36,48[/b]
